research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-ex-r-and-open-interval-homeomorphic-not-uniformly-isomorphic.log:9335:research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log:282329:+- Concrete defects found so far: the library's proper-filter convention makes every uniform space nonempty, but empty metric spaces, empty completely regular spaces, and empty compact Hausdorff spaces are admitted. Consequently the published metric/gauge/cover dictionary and the uniformizable/completely-regular and compact-Hausdorff uniqueness chain contain unqualified empty-carrier failures. Separately, `lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base` is repeatedly cited for square roots and arbitrary finite-composite control absent from its Statement; the minimal-Cauchy-filter construction never establishes that its carrier is nonempty before generating a proper uniformity; `ex-r-and-open-interval-homeomorphic-not-uniformly-isomorphic` attributes a triangle-inequality consequence to `lem-of-abs-value`, whose Statement contains no triangle inequality; and `thm-complete-and-totally-bounded-uniform-spaces-are-compact` cites `thm-ultrafilter-lemma`, whose Statement assumes full Choice, even though `thm-compactness-via-nets-filters-and-ultrafilters` alone states the required ultrafilter-lemma compactness criterion.
