research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-a4-recovery.log-5988-4.1 Step 3.1 says that $\eta$ is injective exactly when $\mathcal U$ is separated. When injective, the two directions of the pullback condition in step 2.1 say precisely that the corestriction $X\to\eta[X]$ and its inverse are uniformly continuous, so $\eta$ is a uniform embedding. Conversely every uniform embedding is injective. [step 2.1, step 3.1, L3, L4]
